From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:28:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(ethereum): allow sub-second negative timeBeforeBlockMs
 in the fee analyzer stats test

The analyzer subtracts the snapshot time (ms) from the mined block's
timestamp (whole seconds), so a block mined in the same second as the
snapshot gives a negative value of up to 1 s. With the test runners'
100 ms viem polling the analyzer sees the very next block of the 1 s
anvil, and the stats test failed whenever that block landed in the
snapshot's second. Assert > -1000 ms, the bound that still shows the
block was mined after the snapshot.

diff --git a/yarn-project/ethereum/src/l1_tx_utils/l1_fee_analyzer.test.ts b/yarn-project/ethereum/src/l1_tx_utils/l1_fee_analyzer.test.ts
index 2465a91e0c9c6ec821b8df0fc221ed982817d0d5..9e09f9ef77430dee5d1331e19e0a842170495f90 100644
--- a/yarn-project/ethereum/src/l1_tx_utils/l1_fee_analyzer.test.ts
+++ b/yarn-project/ethereum/src/l1_tx_utils/l1_fee_analyzer.test.ts
@@ -320,7 +320,10 @@ describe('L1FeeAnalyzer', () => {
 
       const stats = analyzer.getAnalysisStats();
       expect(stats.totalAnalyses).toBe(3);
-      expect(stats.avgTimeBeforeBlockMs).toBeGreaterThan(0);
+      // Block timestamps have whole-second resolution and the snapshot time has millisecond resolution, so a block
+      // mined in the same second as the snapshot yields a negative time of up to 1 s. Anything above -1000 ms still
+      // means every analysis was completed against a block mined after its snapshot.
+      expect(stats.avgTimeBeforeBlockMs).toBeGreaterThan(-1000);
       expect(stats.avgBlobsInBlock).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
       expect(stats.blocksBlobsFull).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
     }, 15000);
